.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.REQUIRES.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.requires.mk
.Nd checks for prerequisite software
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Checks that software a module needs is already there.
It acquires nothing: for that, see
.Va IMPORT
in
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5 .
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Ss Variables
.Bl -tag -width "REQUIRES"
.It Va REQUIRES
Names, checked with
.Ql pkg-config --exists ,
then
.Ql command -v .
An entry
.Cm header: Ns Ar path
is checked by preprocessing an
.Ql #include ,
in C and then in C++, and is also accepted under
.Ar prefix Ns Pa /include
for the prefixes in
.Xr mk.paths 5 .
.El
.Pp
A missing entry stops a module's build when its makefile is read, before any slow
step.
A workspace or framework build checks every module first, and lists everything
missing at once before building anything.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
REQUIRES=cmake gdal header:glm/glm.hpp
\&.include <mk.prog.mk>
.Ed
.Sh CAVEATS
On a cross build with a sysroot, a library is looked for in that sysroot and a
tool on the host's
.Ev PATH .
Without a sysroot, the host is asked, which says nothing about the target.
A
.Cm header:
entry found under a prefix adds no
.Fl I ;
a module that includes it directly still needs one.
There are no version constraints.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bmake-it 7 ,
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5 ,
.Xr pkg-config 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
